+# TypeScript admin SDK
+
+## Purpose
+
+The TypeScript client consumes the versioned REST API. It does not import SvelteKit or server domain implementations and can be used by Node, Bun, edge runtimes, browsers with an authorized proxy/session, scripts, and tests.
+
+## Client model
+
+Construction accepts:
+
+- base URL;
+- AuthFn-compatible authentication provider or explicit header callback;
+- default workspace, project, environment, namespace, and region;
+- fetch implementation;
+- timeout and retry policy;
+- user agent/client metadata;
+- request and correlation ID factories.
+
+Clients are immutable. `client.withScope(...)` returns a new scoped client rather than mutating global state.
+
+## Surfaces
+
+- `client.registry()` discovers enabled capabilities.
+- `client.module(id)` creates a capability-aware dynamic module client.
+- generated or composed typed module accessors expose stable operation methods.
+- `client.pages(...)` and async iterators handle cursor pagination.
+- `client.audit(...)`, `client.search(...)`, and `client.overview()` expose shared platform capabilities.
+- `client.raw(...)` is an escape hatch that still applies authentication, scope, request IDs, errors, and abort behavior.
+
+## Mutations
+
+Mutation options support:
+
+- idempotency key;
+- optimistic version/ETag;
+- explicit confirmation token when required by capability metadata;
+- abort signal and timeout;
+- correlation ID;
+- dry-run only when the domain operation actually supports it.
+
+The returned result exposes `auditId`, `requestId`, replay/deduplication status, and safe warnings in addition to domain data.
+
+## Errors
+
+The SDK throws typed normalized errors with status, code, message, issues, retryability, request ID, audit ID, and safe details. It preserves response access through the raw escape hatch without leaking authentication material into serialization.
+
+Retry policy is conservative:
+
+- safe reads may retry transient connection and dependency failures;
+- mutations retry only when the operation is declared idempotent and an idempotency key is present;
+- authentication, authorization, validation, not-found, and conflict errors are not automatically retried.
